1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,859
A lot of people think this is the best lasagna in New York City.

2
00:00:03,339 --> 00:00:08,099
Freshly boiled house-made lasagna sheets get an ice bath, rinsed, and laid down on a buttered pan.

3
00:00:09,679 --> 00:00:16,260
On goes their bolognese ragu, which gets spread all over, a healthy drizzle of bechamel,

4
00:00:16,859 --> 00:00:17,679
and parmesan cheese.

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:25,760
Another lasagna sheet, more bolognese ragu, more bechamel, more parmesan cheese.

6
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:28,339
They repeat this process two more times.

7
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,660
I could watch them make this lasagna all day long.

8
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:35,159
Notice how they aren't shy with any of the ingredients whatsoever.

9
00:00:38,039 --> 00:00:44,640
And once they finish off this last layer, they rinse and lay down that last lasagna sheet,

10
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:50,359
tuck in the sides, cover it with plastic wrap and foil,

11
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:54,000
then bake it in the oven until it looks like this.

